The publications filter should hide year dividers when only one paper is visible in that year, but filtering “LLM Reasoning and Agency” still showed a divider for 2024.

- Logic: Update `updatePublicationDividers` to detect whether the page has year headers; apply single-item divider removal per year when headers exist, otherwise on the single list (e.g., About).  
- Styles: Existing `.single-pub-in-year` styling now correctly triggers for single visible items after filtering without affecting multi-item years.

Example:
```js
// Per-year handling when year headers are present
const yearHeaders = publicationsSection.querySelectorAll('h2.year');
if (yearHeaders.length > 0) {
  yearHeaders.forEach(header => {
    const list = header.nextElementSibling;
    const visiblePubs = getVisiblePublications(list);
    list.querySelectorAll('li').forEach(li => li.classList.remove('single-pub-in-year'));
    if (visiblePubs.length === 1) visiblePubs[0].classList.add('single-pub-in-year');
  });
  return;
}
```

